  "title": "Design Settings » Header Design | Brilliant Directories Documentation | BD Support",
  "content": "Design Settings » Header Design Link: https://support.brilliantdirectories.com/support/solutions/articles/12000044979 Header Design This article goes over the Header Design settings. Visual Guide of Header Settings To access this section please navigate to : Settings Design Settings General Tab Header Design 1. Display Header Hide or Display the Header, options Yes No 2. Public Header Menu The Public Header Menu is going to show for visitors, of the website: 3. Logged In Header Menu The Logged In Header Menu is going to display only when members are logged in. Important Note Only the default or an exact clone of the Logged In Header Menu is going to work on this area. Other Menus listed on Toolbox >> Menu Manager are not going to work since these are not designed for this area. Use this Menu option to add links just for members. 4. Link & Font Size Change the size of the Header Links 5. Header Menu Item Alignment This setting determines how the navigation links in the website’s header are positioned horizontally. 6. Header Search Module There are several search combinations for this section. For more information about these combinations, review the following support article: Show Header Search 7. Display Translate Tool This tool is an Add-on Google Website Translator 8. Header Background Select the color of the Header Background. 9. Link & Font Color 10. Signup Button Background 11. Font Color The button appears by default on the Header, the link on this button goes to the /join page. 12. Search Button Background 13. Font Color The button displays when a Search Module is selected under Header Colors >> Header Search Module . Header Mobile-View Settings These settings will apply for all mobile devices, with these settings hide or display the following sections: 14. Website Header 15. Website Logo Select how the logo appears on Mobile-View. 16. Mini-Nav Links The options for this section are: Display on Mobile Hide on Mobile Use as Mobile Main Menu 17. Header Search The options for this section are: Display on Mobile Compact on Mobile Hide on Mobile For additional assistance: Email support@brilliantdirectories.com or create a ticket Inside Your Account Dashboard . Was this article helpful and accurate? Yes No Send feedback Sorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
